<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech DEZA CZK 145 mln 1996 net profit.</title>
<headline>Czech DEZA CZK 145 mln 1996 net profit.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited results for year ending December 31, 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Pre-tax profit	    213.541     vs     322.485</p>
<p> After-tax profit	  145.242     vs     216.541</p>
<p> Operational profit	302.401     vs     421.711</p>
<p> Production		3,148.037     vs   3,539.765</p>
<p> Total assets	    3,452.368     vs   3,378.435</p>
<p> Basic capital	   1,101.025     vs   1,101.025</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is Deza a.s., a chemical maker.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement that the fall in profit was due to lower sales and higher write-offs in 1996. Deza had write-offs totalling 270.9 million crowns for the year, up from 225.3 million in 1995. The statement added that market prices for plastic softeners fell in 1996, which also bit into its revenues.</p>
<p>Deza shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
